pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% `output DERIVABLE` used to be guarded by `context.solution_logged` alone,
% which `obji` does not set: it stores the same non-input-entailed
% objective-improving constraint into core without logging a solution. The
% core then contains `~x2`, the output file matches it constraint for
% constraint, and the checker certified `min: x2; x1 v x2` as DERIVING
% `{x1 v x2, ~x2}` — false at x1=0, x2=1. Same proxy-vs-hazard failure mode
% as output_equienumerable_sol_then_obji (ay patch 0002, defect 20 there).
f 1;
obji 1;
output DERIVABLE FILE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
